    "title": "Traveler",
    "year": "2024–2025",
    "detailed_description": "<h2>Problem</h2><p>As someone who is chronically online, I end up stumbling across a whole host of interesting resturants, bars, museums, or little hidden away bookstores on Instagram. These are usually in the form of reels or posts, that I end up saving and storing in an Instagram collection for whenever I want to visit the place. Back in 2025, a few friends and I planned a trip to Istanbul, and an immediate issue arose. I had to go through and manually watch each reel I saved, and pull the places to plan the trip. Traveler was born from a need to simplify this process. One app that can aggregate all the interesting places, and share it with your close friends.</p><h2>Solution</h2><p>It started off with trying to visualize what I wanted from the app. Something that can easily pull from social media platforms like Instagram, TikTok, and Facebook, a way to see the places on a map, and a way to share these with friends. Starting off with these three core features, I began to draft the app.</p><p>Kicking off with some lo-fi sketches then to Figma hi-fi mockups with a complete implementation with login, map, and place management interfaces. I created the core app. This comprised of 4 main pages:</p><ul><li>Feed: A scrollable page to see what all your friends are saving.</li><li>My Places: A page that shows both all the places you have saved, along with a map view to see all your places on a map.</li><li>Friends: A scrollable page to see all of your friends, and see their profiles.</li><li>Profile: A page that shows your stats, and allows you to edit basic user details like username and email.</li></ul><p>To support the app, Supabase was used for both user auth and to host the database. There are plans to migrate to AWS once the app usage significantly increases.</p><h3>Next Steps</h3><p>The key marketing factor is the ability to import places from external sources. For now Google Map Places, Instagram, and Tiktok are planned. Other sources can be requested by users upon the official launch of the app. While this app continues development, the data flow for these features will not be shared here.</p>"
